mod Main do
  -- Operational Perceus RC witness (core-march.md §4.16 — widening slice 11):
  -- the dual-position invariant (B1, specs/perceus-invariants.md §2.1). `s` is
  -- passed to `both` at BOTH an owned position (`a`) and a borrowed position
  -- (`b`, only read via `String.byte_size`), and is dead in `main` after the
  -- call. Perceus must dup `s` EXACTLY ONCE before the call (one balancing
  -- `inc_rc` for the borrowed alias) and dec it exactly once after — zero
  -- dups underflows the refcount (use-after-free the moment `both` returns
  -- `a`, since the caller's binding then reads through a reference the
  -- callee already believed it owned); two dups leaks one reference forever.
  -- Pinned at the TIR level by test/snapshots/perceus/mixed_owned_borrowed_args.expected
  -- (post-Perceus IR: exactly one `inc_rc s` before the call, one `dec_rc`
  -- after) and at the regression level by
  -- test_compiled_dual_position_owned_borrowed (test/test_stdlib_suite.ml).
  --
  -- This golden adds the TWO checks neither of those cover together: (1) the
  -- standard interp==compiled byte-identical output this whole corpus
  -- verifies, and (2) that the compiled binary is ALSO clean under
  -- MARCH_SANITIZE=1 (ASan+UBSan) — no leak, no use-after-free, exit 0 —
  -- verified live (2026-07-11) and documented here since no CI gate runs a
  -- broad sanitizer sweep yet (a noted gap, not built in this docs slice):
  --   MARCH_SANITIZE=1 march --compile g45_dual_position_borrow.march -o g45san
  --   ./g45san   # exit 0, ASan/UBSan silent
  fn both(a : String, b : String, n : Int) : String do
    if String.byte_size(b) > n do
      a
    else
      "short"
    end
  end
  fn main() do
    let s = "hello-world-this-is-a-long-string-" ++ int_to_string(37)
    let r = both(s, s, 1)
    println(r)
    println("done")
  end
end
